{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Obs are done. Blood pressure is 138 over 86, pulse 92, temperature 37.2, sats 98 percent on air.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. What's the problem?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): My eyes have gone yellow, the urine's dark like Coke, and I'm exhausted. Can we just get on with it.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Umm, about a week. Started after we got back.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The N1 was just trucks the whole way, hectic. We ate at the roadside stalls outside Polokwane coming back from Limpopo, and he was alright then.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Others ill?",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ja. Three of them got the runs, and one has gone yellow too.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nausea?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): A bit, after I eat. Not all the time.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Vomiting?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Never.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Abdominal pain?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Not painful.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pale stools? Itching?",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Neither.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alcohol?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I never drink.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chronic illness?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Hypertension. Err, for years.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): What do you take?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): Pharmapres, uh, the amlodipine. Five milligrams, once in the morning.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chest pain with the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): No, not really.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. At the back of my head.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): Cough or shortness of breath? Checking the chest system.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): No cough. Breathing's alright.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Oh, and last year, the work medical, they said my liver test was borderline. Nobody phoned me back.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Sclera are yellow. Abdomen is soft, no guarding. Liver edge is palpable and a bit tender on the right.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Working impression is acute hepatitis, likely from that food. I can't rule out hepatitis A until we see the bloods.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll book liver blood tests and hepatitis serology for today. We might do an ultrasound scan if it does not settle. Come back in a week for the results."
 ],
